    "after_the_run": "a practical candidate goes to the owner, with the recomputed power on the 172 matches and the caveat that E3 was tuned on 135 of them; a test is the owner's decision, nothing is tested otherwise"
  },
  "readings": [
    "Column names. Every E3 column is named <name>@<offset> (t0 = @0, -400 ms = @-400), as A1's vector. The sanitised shooter_by_goal and gk_dist_goal enter as shooter_by_net and gk_dist_net, because control 1 bans the fragment 'goal' in a design column name and C5 lists shooter_by_goal among the G inputs; the values are unchanged.",
    "Missing indicators. dist, angle and shot_x are missing together, exactly where the sanitised shot_ok is 0, so they share one indicator, shot_missing. kp_instance_conf has kp_conf_missing; n_keypoints and n_players are missing only for an unreadable frame and share frame_missing (0 on every population shot at t0, a constant column of zeros). Every indicator is checked to be 1 exactly where its columns are missing.",
    "ball_source one-hot. The levels are none, own (the row's own frame) and one per fallback frame of E3's source order for that offset: at t0 own, m400, m800 (E3 prefers the -400 ms ball, t0's own ball is the last fallback); at -400 ms own, m800. All levels are columns; the L2 penalty handles the redundancy with the intercept.",
    "Spline. A natural cubic spline with 4 df is the truncated-power basis of Hastie, Tibshirani & Friedman (eq. 5.4-5.5) on 5 knots at the 0/25/50/75/100% quantiles of the training fold's non-missing values (R's ns(x, df = 4)), linear beyond the boundary knots; a missing value is imputed with the training-fold mean before the basis.",
    "Standardisation is applied to every design column, z_g_combo, indicators and flags included, with the training fold's mean and population standard deviation; a constant column keeps scale 1.",
    "z_g_combo in results/xgd_a1_ensemble/oof.csv is the mean of logit(stored p) of the two G-combo models that held each shot out (temperature-scaled member outputs, before the ensemble's Platt step). R and every arm refit their own intercept and slope on it, so the ensemble Platt step, an affine map of z, does not change any arm. Each member's epoch and temperature were selected on its held-out fold (scripts/vendor_retrain_g.py), so z carries a little of its own fold's labels; every arm shares that z.",
    "ALL adds, at t0, the sanitised geometry not in G (each with a <column>_missing indicator), the sanitised flags not already encoded (shot_ok is 1 - shot_missing; ball_ok and ball_fallback are the ball one-hot), the sanitation indicators and counts; at -400 ms, the same plus every G input of that offset, dist and angle linear.",
    "GBM inputs are the raw G inputs without the missing indicators (native NaN), z_g_combo first and monotone increasing, the S flags for GS; no spline, imputation or standardisation.",
    "Log-loss clips probabilities to [1e-6, 1 - 1e-6] (xgpoc.eval.calibration.EPS); the calibration slope and intercept are the logistic regression of y on logit(p) with C = 1e6 (xgpoc.eval.calibration.PlattScaler).",
    "The one-sided 95% bound of every arm is the 5th percentile of the bootstrap \u0394LL: a null reads 'no improvement larger than |bound|'. The 95th percentile is reported beside it.",
    "Category \u0394LL intervals restrict the same 2,000 match draws to the category's shots. A shot whose defining E3 input is missing is neither inside nor outside an E3 category.",
    "Control 2's 'Holm detectable rate' is the share of replicates in which Holm over {G, GS} rejects at least one arm (the familywise rate); the per-arm rates are reported beside it.",
    "Control 4: \u03b2 is the negative root of true \u0394LL(\u03b2) = -0.002 (farther shots score less), solved by brentq on [-5, 0]. The \u03b2 = 0 refit is the unpenalised logistic regression of the probabilities p_\u03b2 on [1, z] over the population; (a, b) is R's L2 fit on every shot, mapped to the raw z scale. 'Empirical power of G' is the share of replicates in which G is a Holm 'detectable improvement'. The oracle \u0394LL, LL(p_true) - LL(R out of fold) on each replicate, is a diagnostic only.",
    "Control 3 runs the full read-out of the real run (every arm, the GBM and the categories) on the permuted labels; its criterion is the Holm rejections over {G, GS} only.",
    "Seeds: control 2 default_rng(1), control 4 default_rng(2), control 3 default_rng(0) for the within-match permutation; each replicate draws y* = (rng.random(n) < p) in replicate order."
  ],
